{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB06267 - MONDO_5362",
  "verbalization": "Udenafil is implicated in the pathogenesis of Erectile Dysfunction (disease) through a series of indirect pathways involving psychologic dyspareunia. The evidence suggests that Udenafil, through its indication for Psychologic Dyspareunia, serves as a bridge to Alprostadil, Mirodenafil, and Avanafil, all of which are indicated for Erectile Dysfunction. These compounds are known to act as phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitors, enhancing erectile function by increasing cyclic guanosine monophosphate levels in penile tissues. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Udenafil, via its interaction with psychologic dyspareunia, indirectly influences erectile dysfunction through the pharmacological actions of its indicated compounds. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Udenafil and Erectile Dysfunction, emphasizing the role of psychologic dyspareunia as a mediator in the drug's effect.",
